Migrations for the application schema (runs, messages, and whatever follows).

Not for the demo accounting data. Those tables come from
test_database_resources/*.sql, which the Postgres container runs once on first
start and which `ar-seed` rebuilds on demand. They are disposable fixtures; the
tables defined here hold real state and therefore need versioned, reversible
changes.

Conventions
  - One migration per logical change, with a working downgrade(). A migration
    you cannot reverse is a migration you cannot deploy on a Friday.
  - Migrations are hand-written: there are no ORM models, so
    `--autogenerate` has nothing to diff. Write the ops explicitly.
  - Never edit a migration that has been applied anywhere but your own
    machine. Add a new one instead.

Usage (from the repo root)
  make migration name="add runs table"   create a new revision
  make migrate                           apply everything pending
  make migrate-down                      revert the last one
  make migrate-status                    show current revision + history

The database URL comes from DATABASE_URL via api.settings, not from
alembic.ini. See env.py.
